---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Gravity Cheat Sheet | Free Newton, Einstein, Black Holes"
  description="Complete gravity cheat sheet with Newton, Einstein, and black holes. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Gravity<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Newton, Einstein, and black holes. From classical gravity to general relativity.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Newtonian Gravity</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Universal Gravitation</h3>
        <pre><code>F = GMm/r²
G = 6.674 × 10⁻¹¹ N m²/kg²
g = GM/r² (gravitational field)
PE = -GMm/r (potential energy)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Orbital Mechanics</h3>
        <pre><code>v = √(GM/r) (circular orbit)
T² = (4π²/GM)r³ (Kepler's 3rd law)
Escape velocity&#58; v_e = √(2GM/r)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>General Relativity</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Key Concepts</h3>
        <pre><code>Gravity = curvature of spacetime
Mass-energy curves spacetime
Objects follow geodesics
Time dilation in gravitational fields
Gravitational waves&#58; ripples in spacetime</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Schwarzschild Metric</h3>
        <pre><code>r_s = 2GM/c² (Schwarzschild radius)
For r < r_s&#58; black hole
Time dilation&#58; t' = t√(1 - r_s/r)
Gravitational redshift&#58; z = 1/√(1 - r_s/r) - 1</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Black Holes</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Event horizon&#58; r_s = 2GM/c²
Singularity&#58; r = 0 (infinite density)
Hawking radiation&#58; T = ℏc³/(8πGMk)
Area theorem&#58; area never decreases</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Gravitational Waves</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Speed&#58; c (speed of light)
Polarisation&#58; + and × modes
Strain&#58; h = ΔL/L
Energy flux&#58; F = c³/(16πG)〈ḣ₊² + ḣ×²〉</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
